{:id :EACL-FORMAL-046
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :benchmark
 :seed-or-trace
 "verified-authority/distinct-root-names/equal-normalized-rule-body"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :performance
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 before the canonical root-denotation identity"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datahike :datascript]
 :root-cause
 "The semantic denotation cache key retained the queried root permission name. Two permission roots with identical normalized incoming rule bodies therefore occupied different entries even though their least-fixed-point grants were equal. The cache remained correct, but it could not reuse a shared subgraph across distinct top-level queries and was slower than completed-answer-only caching."
 :fix
 "Compile a root denotation identity from the exact portable indexed rule maps accepted by generated plan certification, remove only the matching root :head, and retain the structural set of resource type, relation entity ids, subject/intermediate types, target relation ids, and target permission nodes. Prove that equal semantic rule bodies preserve equal root grants throughout fixed-point iteration, bridge exact indexed bodies to those semantic bodies under the compiler certificate, and regression-test JVM/CLJS equal-body reuse plus non-collision for changed relations or target nodes."
 :closing-evidence
 ["formal/dafny/RootDenotation.dfy/EquivalentRuleBodiesHaveEqualSemanticDenotations"
